{title: Fairest Lord Jesus}
{artist: Münster Gesangbuch (1677) / Silesian folk tune}
{genre: Hymn}
{flow: Meditative}
{style: Traditional}
{key: F}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}
{score: fairest-lord-jesus.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Fairest Lord [Bb]Jesus
[F]Ruler of all [C]nature
[F]O Thou of God and [Dm]man the [Gm]Son
[F]Thee will I [Bb]cherish
[F]Thee will I [C]honor
Thou, my soul's [F]glory, joy, and [C]crown [F]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Fair are the [Bb]meadows
[F]Fairer still the [C]woodlands
[F]Robed in the blooming [Dm]garb of [Gm]spring
[F]Jesus is [Bb]fairer
[F]Jesus is [C]purer
Who makes the woeful [F]heart to [C]sing [F]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Fair is the [Bb]sunshine
[F]Fairer still the [C]moonlight
[F]And all the twinkling [Dm]starry [Gm]host
[F]Jesus shines [Bb]brighter
[F]Jesus shines [C]purer
Than all the angels [F]heaven can [C]boast [F]
{end_of_verse}
